"Re: The yeoman and Sergeant\nThe Shakespeare Conference: SHK 11.1279 Friday, 23 June 2000.\nFrom: John Ramsay <\nDate: Friday, 23 Jun 2000 00:58:15 -0400\nSubject: 11.1255 Re: The yeoman and Sergeant\nComment: Re: SHK 11.1255 Re: The yeoman and Sergeant\nHi, Sean, the young, mentally disturbed soldier did kill some members of\nthe Quebec Legislative Assembly with his army issue sub-machine gun.\nThe Sergeant at Arms was a Lt Colonel in WWII. He bravely walked into\nthe chamber, persuaded the soldier that he outranked him and got him to\nsurrender the weapon.\nThe Sgt at Arms received a civilian medal to go with his WWII ones and\ndied a few years later.\nThe killer was released last year after serving about 13 years."
