"The opening 2 minutes from the Shaw Movie! Purchase the full DVD now by making a tax deductible contribution to the Shaw Foundation.\nThe opening 2 minutes from the Shaw Movie! Purchase the full DVD now by clicking HERE.\nThe official trailer offers a glimpse at all phases of Coach Shaw\u2019s life from his early coaching career at Pillow Academy, to his 1995 championship run at Jackson Academy, and the rise of Raider Nation that followed.\nCoach Shaw was known for preparing incredibly detailed scouting reports. Special thanks to his former players for digging through their personal scrapbooks and archives to find a few of these treasures. We will be posting new scouting reports here as we absorb them into our\nEvery Jackson Academy football player wants to beat Jackson Prep. Wes Slay, member of Shaw\u2019s 1995 championship team describes the significance of JA\u2019s first ever victory over their cross-town rival.\nTwo of the biggest sports stories in the state of Mississippi during the 1995/96 school year were Coach Sherard Shaw\u2019s championship football team and Mississippi State\u2019s Final Four basketball team.\nCoach Shaw\u2019s time at Jackson Academy spanned 14 years. This document is an internal device being used in the research process to keep key dates and events in focus as the script is written.\nBrent Johnston (a member of the first three Jackson Academy football teams) recalls his senior year when head coach Sammy Dantone took the Raider team to the University of Alabama\nDr. Stephen Lee is a surgeon with Mississippi Ear, Nose & Throat. He is also a 1991 graduate of Jackson Academy high school and former baseball and basketball teammate of Bubba Shaw.\nIt takes resources to properly tell a story like Coach Shaw\u2019s, and those resources primarily come from corporate sponsors. Executive producer Mike Frascogna highlights the benefits to corporate involvement and how it helps benefit the Sherard Shaw Foundation for Pediatric Cancer Research.\nThe producers have deep connections to Jackson Academy and the Shaw family. Coupled with their extensive experience in producing and managing intellectual property, the Frascogna\u2019s were a natural fit for this project.\nExecutive producers Bubba Shaw and Mike Frascogna discuss how your personal knowledge, stories, photographs, and artifacts, as well as your participation on social media can help enrich this project.\nOne of the most exciting elements of the entire Shaw movie project has been released! The \u201ckey art\u201d will be used in a variety of product packaging and promotion (including this website). The original photo of Coach Shaw was from his years at Jackson Academy\nBubba Shaw of the Sherard Shaw Foundation, and Mike Frascogna of Frascogna IP, announce the movie project documenting Coach Sherard Shaw\u2019s life and the 1995 Jackson Academy football team. The project benefits the Sherard Shaw Foundation for Pediatric Cancer Research."
